a primary school teacher who lost all  four limbs to sepsis has returned to the  classroom after being fitted with bionic  arms 47 year old kath tragenna had both  her legs amputated below the knee and  her arms amputated below the elbow in  order to prevent the spread of sepsis  she was prescribed prosthetic arm hooks  but later fundraised enough money for 3d  printed bionic arms impressive cath  joining us now hi car  morning kay  good morning tell me the difference that  these limbs have made to you  oh gosh um well they mean everything to  me  um  you know they've allowed me to function  as a mum to carry out household tasks at  home and  you know they've allowed me to get back  in the classroom and that really does  mean everything  yeah tell us what happened to you kath  november 2019 i was feeling slightly  unwell at school and asked to leave  early  um i thought it was flu just flu-like  symptoms rested for the weekend and  phoned 111 on the sunday afternoon they  decided to send an ambulance to my house  and after that i remember very little my  body went into septic shock i suffered  multiple organ failure had multiple  cardiac arrests and and i was in a coma  for about seven weeks  oh my goodness me um how have you coped  psychologically  well i think it's so important to  maintain a positive mindset  um  you know i am a mum i wanted to play a  full and active role as a mum again but  at times that seemed impossible and i  really had to break it down to small  tiny goals hour by hour almost sometimes  and maintain a positive mindset and kind  of celebrate every small win  each day  okay and what did small wins look like  oh it would be flipping the cap on a  tube of toothpaste you know anything  that i just couldn't do the day before  but helped me regain my independence  and tell me what it's like being back at  school now  oh i mean it's wonderful um children are  so welcoming so enthusiastic  and  yeah i mean teaching's a passion for me  and it's just 